                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "267ce6b7-5445-3cc9-87ea-e0950fe20423",
                        "entry_id": "d0db7475-d55b-361f-ac8c-bb88d5aa40d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To lift with an upward movement of the hands."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0bc9a2f-7ccd-427b-89f5-39a95afb60ba",
                                "sense_id": "267ce6b7-5445-3cc9-87ea-e0950fe20423",
                                "text": "To high heaven, all so softly, / The angels uphand him; / In meads of May flowers / Mild Mary will meet him: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "121908cf-e98b-469b-801f-51e949a589c6",
                                "sense_id": "267ce6b7-5445-3cc9-87ea-e0950fe20423",
                                "text": "But she say sho could uphand anything brought befo' her so I asked her to work on me."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0d1b485d-2749-3bc5-ae9c-732c8ca92471",
                        "entry_id": "d0db7475-d55b-361f-ac8c-bb88d5aa40d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To strike from below with the hand or fist."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "15a2ecd3-cec3-4f91-a1c2-1fb7082a78d7",
                                "sense_id": "0d1b485d-2749-3bc5-ae9c-732c8ca92471",
                                "text": "Before he had hit, she sprang upright, feinted so that Gull's quick blow whooshed harmlessly past her cheek, and uphanded his chin, stunning him and sending him reeling against Kayser, who had stepped back."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79380d54-2a02-39e9-b39f-8a43a56a8657",
                        "entry_id": "d0db7475-d55b-361f-ac8c-bb88d5aa40d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To uphold, promote, or sustain."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a8639ec-423e-4196-84a7-989abdfc33fa",
                                "sense_id": "79380d54-2a02-39e9-b39f-8a43a56a8657",
                                "text": "Aweel, Jock, I'se no say but we've had mony an up an mony a doon i' life, but there's ae comfort whilk uphands me aboon ilka ither thocht, an its e'en this: Ye married yer Elsie, Jock, frae doonright sheer love an naething mair nor less, an Elsie gae her hail heart an its life's bluid to ye whan she gae'd awa her hond."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f306709e-1ae7-4fd4-921b-2c907457f38c",
                                "sense_id": "79380d54-2a02-39e9-b39f-8a43a56a8657",
                                "text": "He's nae Moderate, man; and gin I'm no sair mistaen, he's a wild man himsel, and wull uphand the Veto."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2877902a-5567-4334-ab26-9f0b937fed42",
                                "sense_id": "79380d54-2a02-39e9-b39f-8a43a56a8657",
                                "text": "Some o' Bible words are no' for every-day use, an' ye might have respected the Holy Scripters mair than to use 'em for uphanding o' yer ain mad clavers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c39daadc-3878-4588-ab59-a6d806817d16",
                                "sense_id": "79380d54-2a02-39e9-b39f-8a43a56a8657",
                                "text": "This conduct may probably be uphanded as injurious to my own views ; if it be so, it is at least the natural offspring of my judgment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68a27fd8-5ecb-4fa9-94a4-f6c6b79b9de9",
                                "sense_id": "79380d54-2a02-39e9-b39f-8a43a56a8657",
                                "text": "Sire, the will to dare, their weapons weak, In spirit the State uphanded to success."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26bcf69e-1d4c-4d8b-8e1e-eb6025959af1",
                                "sense_id": "79380d54-2a02-39e9-b39f-8a43a56a8657",
                                "text": "What signifies keeping the poor lassie in a swither? I'se uphand it's been Robertson that learned ye that doctrine."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b8a7aa8-1ff4-388c-b03a-45e6582cdea0",
                        "entry_id": "d0db7475-d55b-361f-ac8c-bb88d5aa40d3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To raise the hands."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc13db11-549d-4a6e-adef-097d5d784a75",
                                "sense_id": "4b8a7aa8-1ff4-388c-b03a-45e6582cdea0",
                                "text": "But the whole thirty-three uphanded and cried, “Mercy, Kamerad '\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
